                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is pretty much a walking simulator. And while walking simulators can be good for their focus on storytelling and exploration, this one doesn't have much of a compelling story to offer. The whole thing is vague and artsy, and while the visuals can be pretty cool, that alone isn't enough to make the game engaging. Some of the design is cryptic, some of it is frustrating, and none of it is particularly compelling. The most interesting idea is that the world around you changes when you look away, but this mechanic is barely explored, and feels like wasted potential. There's not much story or gameplay here, and unless you're specifically into weird, artsy visuals, it's just kind of boring.",
